## Notes from Scott Mackey (not part of the licence terms above)

In plain words: Asqu is free to use, read, change and share. The one thing you
can't do is sell it, or a product built from it, as a rival to Asqu or AsquHub.
Two years after each version comes out, that version is also yours under the
Apache License 2.0, with no such limit.

Your work stays yours. Everything you create or keep with Asqu (your projects,
files and history) belongs to you. Asqu stores it on your own computer and in
the backup places you choose. Asqu never sends your work to Scott Mackey. It
only sends it where you set it up to go: your backup places and, if you add one,
your own decider program (which may pass it to an AI service you choose, under
that service's terms).

Asqu tidies history by itself once a day: tossed Tries are removed 7 days after
tossing, and saves made inside a kept Try 30 days after saving. Kept changes in
the Timeline are never removed. Run `asqu tidy --dry-run` to see what it would
remove. Keep your own backups of anything important.

Questions: https://asqu.dev
